Z||000000||PontaicFiero2M4||10-11-2001||02:02 AM||||I have had my Fiero for about 5 years now, and everything seemed to work great in it....it has no Pwr options, like the Pwr Windows, Door locks, mirrors, or even power steering....but I love it. Recently though, I was working on the Fiero's engine and found that when I was done. The Air Conditioning/heater would not blow. The Fan turned on....but no air was coming into the car. but when the a/c//heater is off, I can feel air from the outside coming inside the car. like being forced in....I was wondering if someone can help me? Does n e 1 think that it can be the blower? If someone can help that would be great!<P>~FieroSal~||||reg||9
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-11-2001||04:33 AM||||When you push in the buttons for the air conditioning, vent , heater, etc., you should immediately her some motors running that are opening up the ducts to either the outside, or to recirculate air inside the car. If that duct doesn't open, you will get no air no way.<P>I figured this out the first time I cranked on the A/C here in sunny (read:hot as blazes) CA and would turn the fan speed to full and hear a roar behind the dash as the motors spun open the ducts in the dash. Then I could feel the ice cold A/C or roasting heater.<P>Check that out...<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||10-11-2001||04:34 AM||||Sounds like you have outside vent only. Is that button stuck/broken?<P>Sly||||reg||1
